      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Without solving"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Can we say the sum and product of the roots of 3x^2 + 7x - 2 = 0 without finding the roots? Yes, the coefficients tell us directly."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "sum of roots",
          "product of roots",
          "forming an equation",
          "sum of squares",
          "difference of roots",
          "sum of cubes",
          "zero constant"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "If alpha and beta are the roots of ax squared plus bx plus c equals 0, then alpha plus beta equals minus b over a.\nThe product alpha times beta equals c over a.\nThe quadratic equation with roots alpha and beta is x squared minus (sum) x plus (product) equals 0.\nAlpha squared plus beta squared equals (alpha plus beta) squared minus 2 alpha beta.\nAlpha minus beta equals the square root of (alpha plus beta) squared minus 4 alpha beta.\nAlpha cubed plus beta cubed equals (alpha plus beta) cubed minus 3 alpha beta (alpha plus beta).\nIf the constant term is zero, one root is zero and the other equals minus b over a."
        }
      },
